//? Title: Reverse-delete forests: actual connectivity decisions and retained edge identities
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given a weighted undirected graph, find minimum-total-weight edges that connect
every original component without cycles. Reverse-delete scans weighted edges
from heaviest to lightest and removes an edge only when the number of connected
components is preserved. Actual native omission decisions retain caller edge
identities, including parallel edges and self-loops. The original weight1,2,8
triangle remains the central worked input.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

The invariant is that the retained graph spans each original connected
component. If omitting an edge preserves the component count, that edge lies on
a retained cycle. The cycle property permits deleting a maximum-weight cycle
edge while preserving some minimum forest. Processing weights in descending
order therefore leaves a minimum spanning forest. This implementation recomputes
connectivity with disjoint sets for each omission. It inspects all E edge slots
in the initial pass and every deletion pass:
$$ \text{edge-slot visits}=E(E+1). $$
\alttext(The actual direct connectivity implementation scans every edge slot in each of E plus one passes.)
Including vertex initialization, work is O(E log E+(E+1)*(V+E alpha(V))). This
is a direct checked implementation, not a dynamic-connectivity data structure.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/reverse_delete_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/reverse_delete.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const std::vector<a::WeightedEdge> e{{0, 1, 1}, {1, 2, 2}, {0, 2, 8}};
    auto t = a::reverse_delete_trace(3, e);
    const auto &s = t.steps[0];
    std::print("| actual original edge id | components without | removed | actual kept mask |\n| ---: | " "---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &v : t.steps) {
        const std::vector<int> retained(v.kept.begin(), v.kept.end());
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | `{}` |\n", v.edge_index,
                   v.components_without, v.removed, retained);
    }
    g::Diagram d(48, 1100);
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual tested original edge id {}", s.edge_index));
    d.node("n1", {5, 0},
           std::format("Actual components without {}", s.components_without));
    d.node("n2", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual removal {}, final weight {}", s.removed,
                       t.forest.total_weight));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/reverse_delete_tiny.svg");
}
```
