> API and interpretation

The result is a forest of all original components, not just the component
containing vertex0. Finite negative weights, self-loops and parallel edge
identities are supported. Equal weights use an explicit input-id tie rule;
another valid minimum forest can have different equal-weight edges. Edge-slot
counters exclude sorting, vertex initialization and disjoint-set internal
operations.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Kruskal, On the Shortest Spanning Subtree of a Graph and the Traveling Salesman Problem (1956)|https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9939-1956-0078686-7]

